        "paragraph": "StringStream is a read/write Stream view over an external String (non-owning — the String must outlive the stream; reset() rewinds the read cursor and clears the String). ServerStream is a write-only Stream that buffers Print output and flushes it in chunks via server.sendContent() on ESP8266WebServer / ESP32 WebServer, so large HTML pages stream out without holding the whole response in RAM (start a chunked/unknown-length response first and call flush() at the end). Both are header-only and non-copyable. For ESPAsyncWebServer use the built-in beginResponseStream() instead.",
